        "problem": "Express $\\frac{-18{x}^{2}-44x-38}{(x-1)(2x+3)^{2}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{-18{x}^{2}-44x-38}{(x-1)(2x+3)^{2}}\\,=-$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x-1$ |  | $2x+3$ |  | $(2x+3)^{2}$ |",
        "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{-18{x}^{2}-44x-38}{(x-1)(2x+3)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{2x+3}+\\frac{C}{(2x+3)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-1)(2x+3)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n-18{x}^{2}-44x-38=A(2x+3)^{2}+B(x-1)(2x+3)+C(x-1).\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-18(1)^{2}-44(1)-38 & =A(2\\cdot 1+3)^{2}+B(1-1)(2\\cdot 1+3)+C(1-1) \\\\ -100 & =A(5)^{2} \\\\ A & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-\\frac{3}{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-18{(-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-44(-\\frac{3}{2})-38 & =A{(2\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{2})+3)}^{2}+B(-\\frac{3}{2}-1)(2\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{2})+3)+C(-\\frac{3}{2}-1) \\\\ -\\frac{25}{2} & =C(-\\frac{5}{2}) \\\\ C & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=0$ and using our values for $A$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-18(0)^{2}-44(0)-38 & =A(2\\cdot 0+3)^{2}+B(0-1)(2\\cdot 0+3)+5(0-1) \\\\ -38 & =(-4)(9)+B(-1)(3)-5 \\\\ -38 & =-41-3B \\\\ B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-18{x}^{2}-44x-38}{(x-1)(2x+3)^{2}}=-\\,\\frac{4}{x-1}-\\,\\frac{1}{2x+3}+\\frac{5}{(2x+3)^{2}}.\n$$",
